opening day for bolden little league  drew in quite the crowd today  as the players stepped back on the field  for more the first time in more than a  year  8 news 9 reporter victoria saha was  there for the event she got the good  assignment today  she joins us live from the newsroom with  more victoria  sasha these young players were stripped  from their passion for baseball last  year when the pandemic  shot everything down and this year they  were able to go back to playing  with some new changes at doodle field  [Music]  opening day at doolittle field came with  a celebration as the bolden little  league baseball team kicks off their  20-21  season the brand new scoreboard was made  possible with a ten thousand dollar  donation from the alpha phi alpha  fraternity  making the comeback on the field extra  special  it hasn't been a tough year and if you  look around you can see the excitement  that the kids have that they're able to  play baseball again and the excitement  was clear brand new uniforms and  equipment ready to be used  i like how we can take turns your  batting  it takes breaks you take breaks so you  don't get overtired  you're playing the teams everybody gets  to have a certain role  in the whole game several members of las  vegas metro police were there and our  very own sheriff lombardo was able to  throw the first  pitch he tells us it's a way for the  west side community to know that law  enforcement  is on their side we want the community  and the kids  in particular to appreciate the cops and  consider them their friend and not their  enemy  this year the league had 130 members but  they made sure to follow covet 19  protocols  so they can have a successful season  being part of the little league baseball  team is something many families in the  west side aren't able to afford but it's  only possible with the help of donations  and sponsors for the 130 players  the sponsors took care of uniforms  equipment and participation fees  in the new